Ìt can be to a degree, but it would require implementing it in each node, and it still is messy, as it can duplicate the resource unnessesarily, atleast in the case of an array:
```gdscript
@export var actions:Array[SetterAction]:
    set(value):
        if Engine.is_editor_hint() && Input.is_key_pressed(KEY_CTRL):
            for action in actions:
                for v in value.size():
                    if action == value[v]:
                        value[v] = value[v].duplicate()
        actions = value
```
